  "body": "## Accepted complete theorem and separate oriented strengthening\n\nHalting of nonnegative configurations on finite loopless simple strongly\nconnected conservative digraphs is NP-complete under polynomial-time\nmany-one reductions. Target: 3000018 / AMR-029-0018. The separately accepted\nappendix proves the same theorem for oriented graphs, with no antiparallel\narcs. In both constructions, deleting the specified root leaves a DAG of\ndepth at most one, and all initial chip counts, including their total, are\npolynomially bounded in the SAT input length. Hardness also holds with unary\nchip encoding.\n\nThe complete analytic proof preserves the modular-bank identity, Boolean/CRT\nclause predicates, actual simple graph construction, legal checkpoint\nschedule and least action, every graph/bit/chip bound, fixed trivial cases,\nand a self-contained NP membership certificate with the necessary additive\none slack. The appendix preserves its separate three-part oriented graph\nconstruction and directed three-cycle preprocessing. Aggregate finite checks\nare supporting metadata only; no omitted executable is needed by the proof.\n\nNP membership and the stable-capacity observation are credited to\nFarrell\u2013Levine, CoEulerian graphs, Section 3 and PDF page 2:\nhttps://arxiv.org/abs/1502.04690v3 . Their Section 3.1 poses the simple case,\nas does the original attributed Egres question:\nhttps://oldlemon.cs.elte.hu/egres/open/Complexity_of_the_halting_problem_for_simple_digraphs .\nThis does not resolve Eulerian-multigraph halting and is separate from\nmultigraph reachability for problem 3000016.\n\n## Distribution and review limits\n\nExactly nine authored proof/appendix/audit/acceptance/status and public-source\nreview or metadata files are added under `unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/3000018/`.\nEditorial changes reconcile acceptance, use public file names, distinguish\nhistorical supporting observations, and bind the distributed mathematical\nfiles exactly. All analytic arguments, edge cases and qualifications remain.\n\nThis AI-assisted, unrefereed edition makes no first-in-literature or\nexhaustive-current-openness claim, and no external human peer-review,\njournal-acceptance, or formal proof-assistant-certification claim. Programs,\nraw generated outputs, datasets, copied third-party source bodies/PDFs/images,\nand private coordination material are excluded. Edition preparation claims\nno new scholarly retrieval, source-file rehash, source inspection, literature\nsearch, or mathematical test rerun.\n\nQUEUE.md and unrelated entries remain unchanged. Editorial preparation adds\nno substantive proof turn and resets no historical accounting. No merge,\nrelease, DOI or outside outreach is requested.\n\nBase commit: `f6caddda8f8be2cdb3e91494325d8f7f365bc3fc`.\n\n## Exact distributed file identities\n\n- `ACCEPTANCE.json`: 3,457 bytes; SHA-256 `ab41c82fd3dec23912bba4c3669483b454434583d05be825857d720617fd7b89`.\n- `MANIFEST.json`: 1,846 bytes; SHA-256 `3fe3ecb307b8ef632594269043750d4535eadac6af77096f5555b8029e7fce82`.\n- `MATHEMATICAL_AUDIT.md`: 17,171 bytes; SHA-256 `6028ff452fa6e49a1cc85a9a01106494dc82c771c4679666e1e602680aa89802`.\n- `MATHEMATICAL_REPORT.md`: 13,502 bytes; SHA-256 `ca97098b22a3841876d3a9f6d66460312b5820cea1f0cacd381e3d16e6abe4c7`.\n- `ORIENTED_APPENDIX.md`: 2,692 bytes; SHA-256 `4550676ad4a0af003ba6ce068c2c63f1c4dabba4840af48b2087adbac6921a73`.\n- `README.md`: 4,559 bytes; SHA-256 `142cba90aaea10baabcba543cbace622940f14b4dd27c490d3982cfc5a7f0892`.\n- `SOURCE_METADATA.json`: 5,211 bytes; SHA-256 `e3b621919293bca1b78f20f1ec378345814bae0cef70bba54732d33f88353ca0`.\n- `SOURCE_REVIEW.md`: 4,720 bytes; SHA-256 `3260858a28a5196690283ea9f00dd0136c1b3137ff58ba14b419e947c88cea44`.\n- `STATUS.json`: 2,311 bytes; SHA-256 `e236b9fe7da5364c06d5e5dc73123d1327eac4f2eb3ae0c1694023453614ec20`.\n\nThe manifest lists nine members and hashes the other eight; this body pins the manifest independently.\n",
